n : 8
len(data) : 10
Symptoms of shock include rapid heartbeat, weak and rapid pulse, shallow and rapid breathing, cold and clammy skin, pale or ashen complexion, confusion or loss of consciousness, weakness, and thirst. These symptoms occur due to inadequate blood flow to the body's vital organs, leading to insufficient oxygen and nutrient supply. It's a life-threatening condition that requires immediate medical attention.
